# PVAS sandbox netpolicy: bridge-allow
#
# Allow all outbound traffic from PVAS sandbox containers.
# Use this for ad-hoc tool scans that need network access (e.g.,
# osv-scanner querying api.osv.dev, or any tool that needs to fetch
# fresh CVE data).
#
# For complete audits, prefer bridge-deny.
# For the driver orchestrator, prefer host (which is what most
# pvas_container.run() invocations use by default).
#
# Applied by tools/pvas_netpolicy.py when a container is launched with
# network_policy="bridge-allow". Currently a no-op (bridge network is
# already unrestricted), but the chain is set up so that future
# CIDR allowlist can be added without changing the policy name.

# Allow all
-A PVAS_BRIDGE_ALLOW_<AUDIT_ID> -j ACCEPT